Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 09:41:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] design: launcher icon dots on a hexagonal grid, nothing
 cut by adaptive masks

The previous snowflake had diagonal arms (about 37 dp) longer than the vertical
ones (32 dp): 4 dots fell outside the 72 dp circle mask and 10 outside the 66 dp
safe zone, and the pattern turned into noise at launcher size.

New foreground: six equal arms, centre dot, two side-dot pairs per arm, 61 dots
of radius 1.85 on a 5-unit hexagonal grid. The farthest dot edge is 31.85 from
the centre (safe zone is 33). Black background and white dots are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JzUdZYkoiPDqL5pBjLSwYm
---
