From 0116828b4771b8c2443e5edb919f8774fd2970f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 09:43:36 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] fix(messages): open a conversation at its newest message
 and size bubbles to the text
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

messages.getHistory was requested with rev=1, which returns the OLDEST messages
first, so opening a long chat showed its beginning and paging walked forward
from there. Now rev=0 (newest first) and the list uses reverseLayout, so the
latest message sits at the bottom and loading more adds older ones above.

- MessagesMapping.kt: MessageItem and the page mapping moved out of the
  network repository so the paging rules are unit-testable without Android.
- PagedColumn: new reverseLayout parameter (pull-to-refresh is off in that mode).
- Bubbles wrap their text (max 82% of the width) instead of always being 88% wide.
- Tests: MessagesMappingTest (6) and a DTO decode test in VkResponseParserTest;
  MessagesMapping is part of tools/verify-core.sh (84 pure-Kotlin tests pass).

Whether VK allows messages.getHistory for the VK ID token is NOT verified here;
the in-app "Проверить доступ к VK API" screen reports the real answer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
