From 2f74ebf8d82472b83dc36064c77dea93a4ddb4ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 07:29:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] fix(auth): sign in through the official VK ID SDK instead
 of legacy VK.login()

The "invalid_request / Security Error" text is not produced by Kontakt or by
com.vk:android-sdk-core 4.1.0 (the string exists in neither source tree), so it is
VK's server answering the request the legacy SDK builds: the implicit flow
(response_type=token) on api.vk.com/oauth/authorize. The official, maintained path
is VK ID SDK 2.7.3 (OAuth 2.1 + PKCE on id.vk.ru), which is what an app registered
in the VK ID cabinet is meant to use.

- Replace com.vk:android-sdk-core with com.vk.id:vkid:2.7.3; add the VK ID
  repositories (the same set that built green in CI before the Standalone detour).
- Remove the classic SDK entirely: VK.setConfig/VK.login, VKKeyValueStorage on
  TokenStore (legacy vk_sdk_ keys are still wiped on clear).
- Do not put client_secret into the APK. VK ID SDK 2.7.3 does not use it for the
  PKCE code exchange; the manifest placeholder only gets a neutral non-secret value.
- Start sign-in from a process-level scope instead of the Activity, so recreating
  the Activity while the VK window is open cannot lose the result.
- AuthFlow (pure Kotlin): one attempt at a time, every outcome clears busy, token
  accepted only after it is saved, 5-minute watchdog for a lost result.
- AuthFailure: map VKIDAuthFail types to clear messages and strip codes, state,
  device_id, tokens and token-like strings from SDK descriptions.
- Request only the base scope by default; scopes that are not enabled for the app
  in the VK ID cabinet invalidate the request.
- Tests: AuthFlowTest (17), AuthFailureTest (11).

Not proven: that this removes the error for the owner's app ID. That can only be
confirmed by signing in on a device.

